# promise: #731
# An extension's toolbar popup runs on the page under its button, with a Little Window open too. Chrome runs a
# triggered action on its window's active tab, not the tab it is asked for, and that tab followed the page Cra last
# focused: the Little Window's, or the blank page that keeps the profile's Chrome window open, which extensions
# can't see. uBlock Lite's popup then said "not a website" over google.com (#731). The fixture popup loads
# page.html?n=popup-context-current-<n>-last-<n> naming the active tab it got ("none": no tab).
budget rss=1100 stalls50=20
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": true, "defaultLinkDestination": {"littleWindow": {}}}
cra://debug?installExtension=${FIXTURES}/PopupContextExtension
relaunch
cra://debug?windowSize=1200x800
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=first
wait 1
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=site
wait 2
# A link from another app opens in a Little Window, whose page takes the focus.
cra://debug?externalURL=${PAGE}?n=little
wait 3
# The main window's button: its page, not the Little Window's.
cra://debug?extensionAction=${POPUP_CONTEXT_EXTENSION_ID}
expect-log "GET /page\.html\?n=popup-context-current-site-last-site HTTP
reject-log "GET /page\.html\?n=popup-context-current-little
